# White Gold Marquise Engagement Ring ({{year}}): 3 Rhodium Issues Over 5 Years

![Three loose marquise cut diamonds held in jeweller tweezers against a soft grey backdrop as the DiamondCritics featured image for the {{year}} white gold marquise engagement ring guide titled 3 rhodium issues over 5 years](/images/white-gold-marquise-engagement-ring.jpg "White Gold Marquise Engagement Ring 3 Rhodium Issues Over 5 Years")

## TL;DR — White Gold Marquise Engagement Ring in One Scroll

**A white gold marquise engagement ring is a 14k or 18k yellow-gold-alloy ring plated with rhodium to achieve a cool white finish.** The look reads as "platinum-adjacent" at a fraction of the platinum price. The hidden cost is maintenance — the rhodium plating wears off over 5 years and must be reapplied for the ring to keep the white-metal look it had on day one. Three rhodium issues cost $150–$300 across the first 5 years and $500+ across the ring's lifetime.

**The 3 rhodium issues over 5 years (all 3 covered in full below):**

- **Issue 1 — Rhodium wears off at high-friction points by year 2.** The shoulders, prong tips, and inside of the band contact fabric and skin daily. The rhodium wears thin at these points first. The yellow undercoat shows through as faint warm patches.
- **Issue 2 — Yellow undercoat shows through at year 3–4.** As rhodium thins across more of the ring surface, the underlying 14k yellow-alloy base becomes visible. The ring reads as "white with yellow casts" — half-white, half-warm. Looks aged.
- **Issue 3 — Full re-plating required at year 5.** Professional re-plating costs $50–$150 per visit. The ring returns to day-one appearance. Repeat every 5 years for life. Lifetime maintenance cost: $500–$1,500+ across 50-year ring life.

→ Entry pick: **[Ten Prong Solitaire in 14k White Gold at $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — market floor, ten-prong max tip protection.
→ Classic pick: **[Petite Solitaire in 14k White Gold at $1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-solitaire-item-194386?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — timeless classic + 1,187 reviews.
→ Hidden halo pick: **[Petite Micropavé Hidden Halo in 14k White Gold at $1,430](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-micropave-hidden-halo-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-5-ct-tw-item-147511?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — micro-pavé + hidden halo.
→ Three-stone pick: **[Marquise Lab Three Stone in 14k White Gold at $1,620 (JA)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/marquise-cut-lab-grown-diamond-three-stone-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315104?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — marquise flankers in matched metal.

**Priority:** G colour centre stone minimum in white gold (vs H-J acceptable in yellow gold). The cool white metal unmasks any warm tint — a J stone that looks fine in yellow gold reads yellow in white gold. Budget for rhodium re-plating every 5 years. See the full [marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond) for shape fundamentals.

## Expert Summary

White gold marquise engagement ring pricing in current certified market inventory starts at **$860** for the Ten Prong Solitaire in 14k White Gold and runs to **$9,115** for the Trapezoid Three Stone in 14k White Gold by Bella Vaughan (single-centre; most 14k white gold settings sit under $5,000). 60 white gold settings across every style. Add a 1ct G-colour marquise centre and the complete ring sits at $1,600–$2,500 for lab, $3,900+ for natural.

I'm Farzana Hasan, a [GIA](https://www.gia.edu/)-certified diamond expert. White gold is the single most popular marquise metal because it reads as "platinum luxury" at $1,000+ less upfront cost. The hidden lifetime cost is rhodium maintenance — a factor many buyers don't factor in before purchase. In 15+ years of grading, I have re-polished and recommended re-plating on hundreds of white gold rings at the 3–5 year mark. Clients who understand the maintenance up front are satisfied. Clients who don't feel ambushed. The 3 Rhodium Issues in this guide are the honest math. Full credentials at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**. Our pillar **[marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond)** covers every related topic.

This guide covers the 3 rhodium issues over 5 years, the Rhodium Wear Timeline, the G-Color Minimum Rule, the Lifetime Replating Cost, 1ct to 2.5ct centre pairing math, and the full white gold marquise inventory from $860 to $9,115 across all setting styles. All prices verified against live certified inventory. Pricing presented as independent market research.

