**Buy the [Marquise Cut Lab Three Stone in 14k White Gold at $1,620 (JA)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/marquise-cut-lab-grown-diamond-three-stone-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315104?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).** Pair with a 1ct G-colour lab marquise around $750. Total: $2,370. Matched marquise flankers + white gold.

## How to Verify a White Gold Marquise Before You Buy

Three checks every ring must pass before you commit.

**Check 1 — Confirm the centre stone colour grade is G minimum.** F for best value, G for minimum safe. Avoid H+ in white gold — switch to yellow gold or platinum if your budget demands H+.

**Check 2 — Confirm V-tip centre prongs at order.** White gold does not change the tip chip risk. V-tip mandatory. $0 extra on most listings.

**Check 3 — Confirm the retailer includes the first free re-plate.** Many major retailers include the first rhodium re-plate free. Confirm this at purchase + factor in the $50–$150 for subsequent re-plates every 5 years. [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) and [GIA 4Cs](https://4cs.gia.edu/) verify loose stones only — the service policy is on the retailer.

I run these three checks before I quote any client on a white gold marquise. All three must pass for the ring to deliver on the long-term value promise.

